ARCHITECTURE (ADR-002/004/005/006/013/014/015)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  - AlertRulesPage (SwiftUI View) + @Observable AlertRulesPageModel. No business
    logic in the view body; all data + selection + rename validation via the model.
  - Data seam AlertRulesDataSource keeps the web hook names verbatim at the Swift
    call sites: useAlertRules (GET /alerts/rules), useBulkEnableRules
    (POST /alerts/rules/bulk/enable), useBulkDisableRules
    (POST /alerts/rules/bulk/disable), useDeleteAlertRule (DELETE /alerts/rules/{id}),
    useSaveAlertRule (PUT /alerts/rules/{id}). Only this file changes when the
    generated client lands (P1/S2-S3). The Sample source is an actor so the bulk /
    delete / rename mutations persist across the model's refetches, like the server.
  - Panels reproduced (every web region, same data + order): the EditConflictBanner
    (AlertRulesEditConflictBanner), the BulkActionToolbar (AlertRulesBulkToolbar:
    pluralized count, Enable/Disable/Delete + destructive-delete confirmation, Clear),
    the GlassPanel1 rules table (AlertRulesTable: select-all + per-row select, the
    EditableText name cell linking to Alert Studio + inline rename, the signal, the
    SeverityBadge + status Badge), and the "Open Alert Studio" footer.
  - Charts/maps: none (web source has none) — N/A.
  - Adaptive: AlertRulesTable renders a column Grid at regular width (macOS/iPad) and
    stacked rule cards at compact width (iPhone) via @Environment(\.horizontalSizeClass).
  - Severity reuses the module's canonical public AlertRuleSeverity (declared in
    feature-views/AlertMessageEditor.Models.swift; web 'info'|'warn'|'critical') with
    a feature-local tone/systemImage extension — DRY, and avoids a duplicate-type
    collision (see VERIFY > BUILD).
  - Units: this page carries no SI physical quantities (rule name / signal name /
    severity / enabled) — the SI converter boundary is N/A here; previews still inject
    .tsUnits(.metric) for consistency with the sibling pages.
  - i18n: AlertRulesStrings (ARStrings) folds the web keys onto the catalog's
    `translation.alertRules.*` / `translation.common.*` / `translation.bulk.*` /
    `translation.editConflict.*` / `translation.editableText.*` entries (ADR-014);
    23 keys pre-existed, +3 added. English fallbacks mirror the web t(key, default).
  - Live data: the rules list is CRUD, not a live stream — no SSE / staleness chip
    (web source has none), consistent with ADR-013 (only live sources surface staleness).
  - a11y: accessibilityLabel on the select-all + per-row checkboxes (web
    bulk.selectAll / alertRules.selectRule + bulk.selectRow), severity badge label,
    .isSelected traits on selected rows, header traits via the shared typography,
    >=44pt controls, light/dark/high-contrast tokens, Dynamic Type (ADR-015).
  - Navigation: typed AlertRulesLink NavigationDestination + AlertRulesRouteRegistration
    .make() factory, mirroring the sibling unrouted DrivingDynamicsRouteRegistration;
    deep link /notifications/rules -> .notifications added to AppRouteParser (like
    /alerts). The .notifications enum host stays owned by the alerts inbox (no
    predecessor bypass, covenant #7).

